## Priority

Weight: the primary tool of a leg 4, a popular secondary 1, any other 0.25. Order: primary legs under the bar and, when the lock is open, the new language come before any secondary leg whatever the score says; the score orders inside each group. The new language is a row of two primary legs from 0 (weight 4, points 170 = 2 x 85, difficulty 60, an estimate: about ten format causes and ten new rules at 3 each), listed only when the lock is open. Points: to the 85% bar. Needs: the findings (lint) or files (format, the groups of the README table) still to win; causes: the largest until the need is met (a rest no cause names is `unclassified`). Difficulty: per cause 1 when its rule exists and is mapped in the catalog, 3 for a new rule, a format gap or an unclassified rest. Score: weight x points / difficulty. A leg at the bar is not listed.

| Language | Leg | Weight | Now | Points | Needs | Causes | Difficulty | Score | Measured on |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Alpha | lint Lint | 4 | 50.0% | 35.0 | 35 findings | `mapped-rule` 30, `unmapped-rule` 15 | 4 | 35.00 | abc123 |
| Alpha | format Fmt | 4 | 55.9% | 29.1 | 33 files | `big` 30, `small` 5 | 6 | 19.43 | - |
| (not in support.yaml) | lint unlisted | 0.25 | 10.0% | 75.0 | 75 findings | `y` 90 | 3 | 6.25 | abc123 |
| Alpha | lint Pop | 1 | 70.0% | 15.0 | 15 findings | `x` 30 | 3 | 5.00 | abc123 |

